    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d614">

                <pb facs="0679" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.116/72</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to the Chinese
                        Legation</hi><anchor n="89" xml:id="d614-f1"/></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        type="received-date" when="1933-08-14">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>The American Government is very unfavorably impressed by the action and attitude
                    of the Cantonese authorities in what those authorities allege to be regulation
                    of importation and sale of kerosene and by the lack of resolute and effective
                    action on the part of the Chinese Government in connection therewith. The action
                    of the Chinese <pb facs="0680" n="578" xml:id="pg578"/> authorities at Canton is
                    plainly in violation of treaty provisions, and the tactics which they are
                    employing are inconsistent with principles and practices of international amity
                    and peaceful and fair international intercourse. The American Government expects
                    of the Chinese Government and of the Chinese authorities at Canton immediate and
                    effective attention to the representations which are being rightfully and
                    properly made by American officials in China in reference to this situation.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d614-f1" n="89" type="source" xml:id="d614-f1-content">
                <p>Handed to the Chinese Minister August 14.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
